<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edwin of Northumbria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 586–633</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Saint Edwin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edwin of Northumbria was king of Deira and Bernicia from 616 and the most powerful ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> of his day. Around 617 he seized the British kingdom of Elmet and expelled its king Ceretic. Converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> by Paulinus in 627, he was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hatfield-chase">Battle of Hatfield Chase</a> in 633 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadwallon-ap-cadfan">Cadwallon ap Cadfan</a> of Gwynedd and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edwin-of-northumbria.jpg" alt="Edwin of Northumbria" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DaveWebster14 · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_King_Edwin_of_Northumbria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
